    "chunk_text": "2.(1) From and after the date of commencement of thisAct, such and so many persons as now are members of theGreat Wall of Nibbana Development Foundation (hereinafterreferred to as the \u201cFoundation\u201d) or shall hereafter be admittedas members of the Corporation hereby constituted, shall be abody corporate with perpetual succession, under the name andstyle of the \u201cGreat Wall of Nibbana Development Foundation\u201d(hereinafter referred to as the \u201cCorporation\u201d) and by that namemay sue and be sued, with full power and authority to haveand use a common seal and to alter the same at its pleasure.\n\nShort title.\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\nPL 005389 \u2014 300 (8/2017)\n\nIncorporation ofthe Great Wallof NibbanaDevelopmentFoundation.\n\nPreamble.\n\nGreat Wall of Nibbana DevelopmentFoundation (Incorporation)2\n\n(2) The Corporation shall be deemed to be a voluntarysocial service orgonization within the meaning, and for thepurpose of the Voluntary Social Service Orgonizations(Registration and Supervision) Act, No. 31 of 1980 and theprovisions of that Act shall apply to and in relation to themanagement of the affairs of the Corporation.\n\n3.(1) The general objects for which the Corporation isconstituted are hereby declared to be:\u2014\n\n(a)to develop the Buddhist Religious Centres;\n\n(b)to ordain novices in order to uplift the BuddhaSasana;\n\n(c)to nourish laymen with knowlegde of Buddhism andto disseminate religion through them;\n\n(d)to build a multi religious reconciled society pioneeredby Buddhism;\n\n(e)to initiate a rural development program based onreligious guidance;\n\n(f)to contirbute to conserve biodiversity, naturalresources in government and other developmentactivities;\n\n(g)to protect, pormote and uplift religious education;\n\n(h)to preserve and improve religious places; and\n\n(i) to do all such other acts and things as are necessaryfor and incidental or conducive to the attainment allor any of the objects.\n\n(2) In the implementation of the objects specified insubsection (1) the Corporation shall ensure that such\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20"
