    "md5": "b59a462fd554b7c0253dba85d3519c4f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1938,
    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Bill No. 179]\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by the Minister of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Developmenton 23rd of May, 2017\n\n(Published in the Gazette on February 20, 2017)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 6.00Postage : Rs. 10.00\n\n2-2d\n\n2-\n\nFISHERIES AND AQUATIC RESOURCES(AMENDMENT)\n\nto amend the Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Act, No. 2 of 1996\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2: This clause amends section 28 of the Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Act, No.2 of 1996 (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) by the introduction of newsection 28A and the legal effect of the new section is to prohibit, fishing operations utilizingTrawl Nets towed by motorized or mechanized fishing boats and the sale, import andtransport of such nets and the issuance of license relating to utilization of such nets.\n\nClause 3: This clause amends section 49 of the principal enactment by the addition of anew subsection which makes it an offence to contravene the provisions of section 28A.\n\nClause 4: This clause amends section 66 of the principal enactment by the introductionof a definition for the expression \u201cTrawl Net\u201d.\n\nClause 5: This clause amends all the laws which are contrary to the content of theprovisions of section 28A, making section 28A to prevail over such laws.\n\n1Fisheries and Aquatic Resources (Amendment)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n2\u2014PL 005011\u2014475 (02/2017)\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 21/2016.\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE FISHERIES AND AQUATIC RESOURCESACT, NO. 2 OF 1996\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Fisheries and AquaticResources (Amendment) Act, No. of 2017."
  },
