    "chunk_size_bytes": 1795,
    "chunk_text": "AN ACT TO AMEND THE FISHERIES AND AQUATIC RESOURCESACT, NO. 2 OF 1996\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Fisheries and AquaticResources (Amendment) Act, No. of 2017.\n\n28A. (1) (a) No person shall engage in orcause any other person to be engaged in fishingoperations utilizing Trawl Nets, including netswithout two wings or using vertical poles atthe two free ends of the net, to be towed bymotorized or mechanized fishing boats.\n\n(b) No person shall use, possess, import,transport, purchase or sell any Trawl Net, to betowed by a motorized or mechanized fishingboat for the purpose of carrying out fishingoperations in Sri Lanka Waters.\n\n(2) No license shall be issued by theDirector-General under Part II of this Act forfishing operations carried out by Trawl Nets tobe towed by a motorized or mechanized fishingboat in Sri Lanka Waters.\n\nShort title.\n\nInsertion ofnew section28A in theprincipalenactment.\n\n\u201cProhibitionof fishingoperationsutilizingTrawl Nets.\n\nFisheries and Aquatic Resources (Amendment)2\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n(3) Any license, issued under this Act forfishing operations carried out utilizing TrawlNets towed by motorized or mechanizedfishing boats in Sri Lanka Waters, shall not berenewed:\n\nProvided that, a license already issued for theuse of Trawl Nets and which is still in force onthe day preceding the date of commencementof this Act, shall notwithstanding anything tothe contrary in this Act, continue to be validfor the purpose and in respect of which thelicense has been issued, for the period specifiedtherein.\u201d.\n\n3.Section 49 of the principal enactment is herebyamended by the insertion immediately after subsection (2A)thereof, of the following new subsection:\u2014"
