    "chunk_text": "(3) The Minister shall, prior to the ceasing of theoperation of the Parts referred to in subsection (3), by Orderpublished in the Gazette, provide for the transfer to agovernment department or statutory corporation, of theproperty, staff, contracts, assets and liabilities and legalproceedings instituted by, or against, any Agency, Board orother institution established by or under any of those Partsof this Act.\n\nShort title,date ofoperationand durationof this Act.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nPART I\n\nCHAPTER 1\n\nPOLICY DEVELOPMENT\n\n2. (1) There shall be established a Policy DevelopmentOffice to assist the Minister.\n\n(2) The Policy Development Office shall, upon beingrequested by the Minister, have an expert committeefunctioning under the office, prepare a report on \u2013\n\n(a)policy development;\n\n(b)policy review; and\n\n(c)resource allocation,\n\nand submit it to the Minister who may forward the same tothe Cabinet of Ministers with or without his observationsthereon.\n\n3.(1) There shall be a Head of the Policy DevelopmentOffice who shall be a person professionally qualified andexperienced as prescribed, in policy development andimplementation.\n\n(2) The Head of the Policy Development Office shall bethe Chief Executive Officer and shall be responsible forcarrying out all such duties necessary for the managementand administration of the affairs of such Office.\n\n4.(1) The Minister may appoint such officers andservants as the Minister may deem necessary for the properand efficient discharge of the functions of the PolicyDevelopment Office.\n\n(2) Subject to the other provisions of this Act, the Ministermay \u2013\n\n(a)exercise disciplinary control over or dismiss, anyofficer or servant of the Policy Development Office;\n\nEstablishmentof a PolicyDevelopmentOffice.\n\nAppointmentof Head ofthe PolicyDevelopmentOffice.\n\nStaff of thePolicyDevelopmentOffice.\n\n30\n\n3Development (Special Provisions)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n(b)fix the wages or salaries or other remuneration ofsuch officers and servants; and"
